  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The distance between the centre of planet X and the centre of planet Y is 9<em>R</em>. The mass of planet X is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M_{X}\"></span> and the mass of planet Y is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M_{Y}\"></span>. The two planets have the same average density. Point B is located between planet X and planet Y at distance <em>R</em> from planet Y. At point B the total gravitational potential due to the two planets has a maximum value. </p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>What is the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Radius  of  planet  X}{Radius  of  planet  Y}\"></span> ?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">2</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">4</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">8</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">64</li>\n</ol>"
